// A phase is attested and nothing is checked.
//
// `phase` declares `kinds="design-ux · design-system · implement · learn · teach"` as a PROSE
// STRING and carries no fields. So every phase in this record is a `produced=` sentence
// written by whoever closed the iteration, at close, about work already finished.
//
// Read them and the pattern is unmistakable: every `design-system` in this frame is a
// past-tense summary of what was built. ITER.260822.13's said "only the head of a chain is
// checked" — a decision made DURING implementation, attested as a design phase, and wrong.
// The better approach existed and arrived in conversation after the code shipped.
//
// And every `teach` names a skill. A skill is doctrine for an AGENT. The reader of a release
// — who wants the feature's why and how — has been served by the teach phase zero times,
// while the same skill file was counted again as the doctrine LAYER in the same iteration.

thin-slice "TS.260821.19" {
    slug "design-before-implement"
    title "Make a phase produce something, before the next one may start"
    kind "command"
    realizes "CAP.claim-settlement"
    from-storm "ES.260819.01"

    command "close"
    actor "whoever works an iteration, at the moment they reach for the editor"
    produces-event "PlanRecorded" "UnplannedImplementRefused"
    needs-read-model "what-this-iteration-claims-and-has-shown"

    trigger "an iteration starts implementing, and the approach is being decided in the code"
    outcome "design-system produces an approach that exists before implement starts, and teach produces what an end user reads"

    scenario #"""
        Given an iteration whose design-system phase is marked complete
        When implement is marked complete
        Then the record holds the approach design-system produced, what it was chosen OVER, and
             the implement phase names it — because deriving the better approach is what the
             phase is for, and an approach written at close is a description of what was built
             rather than a choice that shaped it.
        """#

    step "1" does="`phase` gets a shape. Its kinds become a checked vocabulary rather than a prose string, which is the fifth decorative declaration this session"
    step "2" does="design-system produces an `approach` — what will be built, and what it was chosen OVER. The alternative is the half that proves a choice was made"
    step "3" does="implement names the approach it followed. An implement complete against a design-system with no approach is REFUSED"
    step "4" does="an approach may be superseded mid-iteration, by maturing it. Discovering the design was wrong while building is the normal case and must stay cheap"
    step "5" does="teach produces what the END USER reads — the version's docs, the feature's why and how. A skill is the doctrine LAYER, and counting one artifact as both is what hid this"

    excludes "a separate design document. The approach lives in the iteration, beside the claims \
        it will settle. A file elsewhere is a second thing to keep in step, and the record already \
        holds thirty-four slices whose scenario and steps are exactly this shape"
    excludes "an approval gate between design and implement. The same agent may do both — what is \
        refused is implementing with NO approach recorded, not implementing without permission. \
        Self-approval is TS.260821.08's subject and it is a different rule"
    excludes "forcing design-system on every slice. A slice whose layers do not need it skips it, \
        with a reason — skipped-phase-without-rationale already exists and is unwitnessed"

    layer "doctrine"    reaches="the phases say what each must produce, and teach says for whom"
    layer "enforcement" reaches="implement complete with no approach is refused; a teach naming only a skill is reported"
    layer "docs"        reaches="`what did they consider, and why this` is answerable per iteration"

    claim "C1" text="design-system produces an approach naming what it was chosen over" \
        settled-by="a test asserting an approach with no alternative is refused — a choice with nothing rejected is a description of the only thing anybody thought of"
    claim "C2" text="implement complete against a design-system with no approach is refused" \
        settled-by="a test marking implement complete with the approach absent, asserting a refusal that names the phase rather than the rule"
    claim "C3" text="an approach can be superseded while the iteration is open" \
        settled-by="a test maturing an approach mid-iteration and asserting the close accepts it — discovering the design was wrong while building is the normal case, and a rule that punishes it teaches people to write the approach afterwards"
    claim "C4" text="teach produces what an end user reads, and a skill alone does not satisfy it" \
        settled-by="a test asserting a teach phase producing only a path under skills/ is reported, and one naming the version's published set is not"
    claim "C5" text="the phase vocabulary is checked rather than described" \
        settled-by="a test asserting a phase of an undeclared kind is refused — `kinds=` has been a prose string for the whole life of the record"

    depends-on "TS.260821.18 — an approach that turns out wrong is matured, not overwritten"

    useful-alone "the phase that exists to derive a better approach starts producing one. Every \
        design-system in this record is a past-tense summary of what was built, written at close \
        by whoever built it, and one of them was wrong in a way the phase existed to catch"

    attacks "S3"

    useful-to "the-team-building-a-digital-product" "the-reader-of-a-release"

    cut-from "the maintainer, on ADR.260819.02's phase list: a thin-slice needs an implementation \
        plan so the better approach is derived before it is implemented"

    principle-note "how much process a unit of work received is declared by the agent that received \
        it — that is S3, and the phases are where this record has been doing it to itself. Five \
        phases, attested complete on every iteration, with nothing checked about any of them. The \
        one that was wrong was wrong in exactly the way a design phase exists to prevent"

    proves "an approach existed before the code did, and says what it was chosen over"
    does-not-prove "that the approach was good. It makes the choice visible and contradictable — \
        a bad approach recorded beats a better one nobody wrote down, because only the first can \
        be argued with before it ships"
}
